  1517	
  1518	  Description [Mode 1 is the classic map -f guard. Mode 2 is the stmap1
  1519	  selective guard, which only rejects wider cuts when the node has higher
  1520	  estimated fanout. Mode 3 is the stmap2 guard, which uses the same fanout
  1521	  thresholds only during area recovery and only when the current phase has
  1522	  slack over the mapper required time. Mode 4 is the stmap3 guard, which
  1523	  narrows the intervention to high-fanout nodes with only shallow positive
  1524	  slack. Mode 5 is the stmap4 split-phase guard: stmap1-style guarding in
  1525	  delay matching and stmap2-style slack-aware guarding in area recovery.
  1526	  Mode 6 is the stmap5 shape-gated split-phase guard: the delay pass only
  1527	  uses stmap1-style guarding in very large mapper graphs, while area recovery
  1528	  keeps the stmap2 slack-aware guard. Mode 7 is the stmap6 area-sensitive
  1529	  shape-gated guard: the delay pass keeps the stmap5 graph-size gate, small
  1530	  mapper graphs keep the stmap2 slack-aware recovery guard, and exact-area
  1531	  recovery on larger graphs checks the cut after matching so materially cheaper
  1532	  cuts can override the fanout/load proxy. Mode 8 is the stmap7 criticality-
  1533	  sensitive version of mode 7: exact-area recovery on larger graphs allows the
  1534	  override only with deeper mapper slack and outside the highest fanout bucket.
  1535	  Mode 9 is the stmap8 arrival-bounded version of mode 8: the area-saving
